{
  "abstract": "We construct an ordinary vector bundle on a smooth projective variety whose semiregularity map is injective on the image of Hochschild evaluation, whose rational Chern classes remain Hodge along an algebraic family, and which has a first-order lift but no second-order lift for any first-order choice. This gives a negative answer to Markman's weak semiregularity Question 11.4, including its untwisted version on a projective bundle over an abelian eightfold. We first construct a twisted example in a polarized abelian scheme of relative dimension eight, with polarization type $(1,1,1,1,15,15,15,15)$ and an algebraic finite gerbe. An explicit Clifford calculation identifies the ample class preserved by its obstructed ordinary tangent. The local tensor Hodge locus in weight one is smooth; Cattani–Deligne–Kaplan provides an algebraic curve with the same tangent, and finite-coefficient cohomology extends the gerbe. Gabber's Azumaya theorem supplies a relative Brauer–Severi variety on which the bundle becomes untwisted. An admissible embedding preserves semiregularity on the entire ambient Hochschild evaluation image, while its global right adjoint sends every hypothetical second-order lift back to an excluded twisted lift. The source remains a rank-two Horrocks–Mumford pullback with an exact categorical obstruction, a stable surface companion and uniform cohomology giving a coherent Orlov image. The untwisted central variety is a projective bundle over an abelian eightfold, of unspecified larger dimension. These are obstructions to transporting particular bundles, not counterexamples to the rational Hodge conjecture.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
  "change_summary": "Extend version2 to a fixed polarized algebraic abelian family with an algebraic finite gerbe, then obtain an untwisted example on a relative Brauer–Severi variety. New Sections7.3–7.5 prove preservation of the explicit ample class, exact local linearity and CDK algebraization of the Hodge locus, finite-gerbe extension, preservation of weak image semiregularity under an admissible embedding, and obstruction transport by a global right adjoint. Add a full-Fock linear algebra checker. All accepted source/coherence code and data remain unchanged. No untwisted abelian example or HC counterexample is asserted. The independent audit is addressed by explicitly identifying the central root-gerbe categorical evaluation and semiregularity maps through tensor equivalence; the untwisted scope is stated in the opening paragraph and abstract.",
